<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nyanza, Rwanda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nyanza is a town in the Southern Province of Rwanda that became the permanent royal capital under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuhi-v-musinga">Yuhi V Musinga</a> around 1899. Until then the court had moved between residences. A reconstruction of the traditional royal palace and the palace built for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutara-iii-rudahigwa">Mutara III Rudahigwa</a> in the 1930s are now museums, and the tombs of Mutara III and Kigeli V are nearby at Mwima.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nyanza-rwanda.jpg" alt="Nyanza, Rwanda" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guswen · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King%27s_palace_in_Nyanza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
